## Finding

``` text
head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/openai_streaming.py:227 — The reasoning-delta handling only works when the server leaves `content` out of the delta. Many local OpenAI-compatible servers (Ollama's `reasoning`, LM Studio and llama.cpp builds) send `"content": ""` next to every reasoning chunk. That empty string is still passed to `_recovery_feed_openai`, so `on_token("")` counts it toward the 200-token `empty_content_window`, and the stream is aborted (`StreamingRecoveryAbort: empty_content_window`) before the model finishes thinking. This defeats the `on_progress` design (D-7.3). The new tests (`test_openai_thinking_strip.py`) only build deltas without a `content` key, so they miss it. Skip the empty-content feed when the same delta carried a reasoning trace.
head/.claude/scripts/lib/hop-locality.py:116 — A hop counts as "local" purely because its config declares `dispatch_group: local` (on the model entry or, via `or block.get("dispatch_group")`, the provider block). Nothing checks that the endpoint is actually loopback/RFC1918 or carries the `allow_insecure_endpoint` opt-in. A project overlay such as `hounfour.providers.openai.dispatch_group: local` therefore makes every api.openai.com hop pass the `local_voices` plan-time filter in adversarial-review.sh and flatline-orchestrator.sh, so the posture's "model calls stay local" promise is not enforced. The provider-level fallback also disagrees with cheval: `modelinv.hop_locality_of` and `OpenAIAdapter._transport_pol …
